Prompt:

Theme: {automotive / travel / sport / urban / photography / etc.}
Brand / Event: {name}
Main word: {short bold keyword}
Person: {adult character, outfit, vibe}
Interactive object: {steering wheel / suitcase / barbell / phone / camera / etc.}
Action: {natural interaction}
Typography color: {acid lime / orange / vermilion / violet / cyan / etc.}
Environment: {car / terminal / gym / metro / street / etc.}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a clean full-bleed editorial campaign poster with realistic photography, oversized colored typography, and strong connected forced perspective.

The foreground object must be the same object the person is naturally holding, operating, pulling, or using. Keep a clear physical connection:

body → arm → hand → object.

Use a 20–28mm wide-angle perspective. The object appears oversized only because it is extremely close to the camera. Keep the grip, anatomy, object structure, and perspective realistic.

Place one huge condensed sans-serif keyword behind the subject using the selected bold color. Let the person, arm, and foreground object naturally overlap the letters to create depth.

Use a continuous full-bleed environment from top to bottom. The street, floor, vehicle interior, terminal, gym, or architecture should extend all the way to the bottom edge.

Do not add a separate footer band. Place bottom text directly over the scene.

Keep supporting information minimal and meaningful: brand, date, location, category, short specs, or action phrases.

Keep the person clean, sharp, and realistic with even skin tone, subtle pores, soft directional light, and natural matte-to-satin skin. Keep the face, hands, and foreground object sufficiently clear.

Avoid duplicated or floating objects, disconnected limbs, incorrect grips, distorted anatomy, oily or blotchy skin, excessive decoration, meaningless filler text, complex UI, CGI skin, and bottom footer bands.

Final result: a bold full-bleed poster with strong color identity, realistic connected action, dramatic depth, and high visual impact.

Prompt:

[Product type]: {sparkling tea / cold brew / smoothie / dessert drink / other}
[Brand name]: {original fictional brand}
[Product name]: {original product name}
[Flavor]: {fruit, tea, dairy, herbs, or other ingredients}
[Main headline]: {a short original two-word phrase}
[Model]: {young adult woman, appearance, hairstyle, expression}
[Pose]: {sitting, leaning, crouching, half-standing, or another interaction}
[Outfit]: {youthful fashion styling}
[Color palette]: {main color + neutral color + accent color}
[Decorative ingredients]: {fruit, flowers, herbs, ice, leaves, or food materials}
[Atmosphere]: {sunlight, mist, bubbles, reflections, condensation, or other}
[Aspect ratio]: 9:16

Create the final image directly as a premium vertical fashion campaign for an original trendy drink or food brand.

Turn the product into an oversized installation occupying around 40–50% of the frame. The young adult model should interact naturally with it by sitting, leaning, stepping, or balancing on the packaging. Show believable weight, contact, perspective, and body proportions. Her appearance should feel youthful, sweet, bright, and photorealistic, with natural skin texture, realistic hair, and an expressive gaze slightly toward the camera.

Use a different pose for each image so the series does not feel repetitive. Keep the product and model as the clear primary subjects.

Place fruit, flowers, herbs, ice, leaves, or other flavor ingredients around the foreground and lower edges. These elements should enrich the scene but remain secondary, occupying only about 10–15% of the visual attention. Use partial cropping and soft foreground blur to create depth.

Add one oversized two-word headline behind the model and product. Give the typography a material effect inspired by the flavor: translucent glass, jelly, acrylic, condensation, bubbles, soft gradients, refraction, or glossy highlights. Let parts of the letters overlap naturally with the model and product to create spatial depth.

Do not use “VOL.1,” “ISSUE 01,” decorative numbering, or generic template labels. Add 3–5 pieces of short original brand copy and arrange them asymmetrically along the frame edge, product contour, light direction, or circular graphic elements.

Use a clean high-key studio environment, a soft color-gradient background, subtle reflective flooring, controlled sunlight, and a product-specific atmospheric effect. Keep the layout rich but uncluttered.

Photorealistic commercial photography, premium editorial styling, realistic liquid, ice, fruit, condensation, packaging materials, natural skin, accurate hands and feet, strong visual hierarchy, refined typography, and polished advertising quality.

Prompt:

Theme: {fashion / sport / music / lifestyle / etc.}
Brand / Event: {name}
Main word: {4–8 letter keyword}
Person: {age, gender, outfit, vibe}
Held object: {bag / helmet / vinyl / bouquet / etc.}
Accent color: {color}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a bold editorial poster combining realistic photography, oversized typography, and connected forced perspective.

The person must physically hold or control the foreground object. Keep one continuous, believable perspective chain:

body → shoulder → arm → wrist → hand → grip point → object.

The same object being held should extend naturally toward the camera and appear oversized only because it is very close to the lens. Do not place a separate oversized object in the foreground.

Use a low-angle wide-lens perspective with the person slightly farther back and the hand/object closest to camera. Keep the grip, fingers, arm, and object physically connected and anatomically correct.

Place a huge condensed sans-serif keyword behind the person, partially covered by the body, arm, and object to create real depth.

Add small editorial information around the edges using meaningful brand, event, product, date, location, or specification details.

Use a warm off-white paper background, subtle print grain, mostly black typography, and one restrained accent color.

Keep the composition clean, fashion-forward, realistic, and dimensional.

